\subsection{Transverse wave correction on the moving vessel}
\label{sec:transverse-wave-replay}
A separate paired experiment held the two-frame geometry fixed and changed
the horizontal observation. The independent-axis and shared-mode CARMA
filters both estimate the transverse encounter time scale from the ratio of
the centered displacement and velocity variances across the estimated wave
axis. After four cycles with live bias learning and a usable wave axis, they
use that time scale in a scalar integral--velocity observation. A change of
CARMA parameters transports the displacement primitive and its covariance
to the new realization. This experiment measures the combined effect of the
observation and that transport.

Six sensor draws on the same 16 moving-vessel records gave 96 pairs per
filter. Pooled 3-D displacement RMS over 300--1,200 s fell from 0.22223
to 0.21884 m for independent axes and from 0.20187 to 0.19852 m for shared
modes. At 40--60 s the differences were below 0.000001 m. On two further
sensor draws reserved until the implementation was fixed, late 3-D RMS
fell in 30 of 32 pairs for each filter. Across all eight draws each filter
also had two head-sea records with an increase above 0.5\% in 3-D
accelerometer-bias RMS. The
\href{https://github.com/bareboat-necessities/ocean-imu/tree/e663f0e6b7cf4df9f23727ed80bcf8d81404d3e2/reports/results/startup_learning/tfg_carma_horizontal_wave/windowed}{paired records and native logs}
give the individual gains and losses.
